window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y1v4-index"]=[{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner","w":"karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 1  karuizawa kei s soliloquy volume cold open  karuizawa s first person soliloquy  alone post shower at the mirror  no other character appears  and p 11 carries no prose   in the end  nothing changed even after i came to this school   no  that s wrong  maybe i never had any intention of changing   my life was destroyed because of that nightmarish day  i lost my youth  my friends  and even myself   the most important thing is protecting myself  i ll do whatever it takes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\">Ch.1: Karuizawa Kei’s Soliloquy<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.10–11<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volume cold open: Karuizawa’s first-person soliloquy, alone post-shower at the mirror; no other character appears, and p.11 carries no prose.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “In the end, nothing changed even after I came to this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “No, that’s wrong… Maybe I never had any intention of changing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “My life was destroyed because of that nightmarish day. I lost my youth, my friends, and even myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Opens by measuring herself against the class: she is certain “none of the boys or girls like me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Claims the knowing no longer hurts, then turns it outward: “Because for some reason, I want them to feel that way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> At the mirror she grips the sink and vomits at “that old wound on my side” — the page ties her self-loathing to an unnamed past and never says what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “The most important thing is protecting myself. I’ll do whatever it takes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Closing self-assessment: “I’m a parasite, a weak creature that can’t survive on its own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Translation defect kept as printed: “Why did I have to have to go through” — the verb is doubled.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank/short scan page: running footer only; no prose to cite.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 0  the cabin reverie and the horikita bridge three days after the island test  the cruise ship respite  ayanokoji s cabin reverie  hirata s interruption  and the deck lunch that follows   sigh  if only i had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself   i ll pass  i don t think i m on especially good terms with karuizawa s group   well  i don t particularly dislike the idea  but  didn t you already promise karuizawa   but even if i can bring you both together  things won t be that easy  horikita is difficult","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three days after the island test, the cruise-ship respite; Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie, Hirata’s interruption, and the deck lunch that follows.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sigh. If only I had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself…”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’ll pass. I don’t think I’m on especially good terms with Karuizawa’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, I don’t particularly dislike the idea, but… Didn’t you already promise Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The rule he entered school under: “Contact with anyone outside is forbidden until graduation.” Chabashira’s leverage rides on it — she threatened to expel him from this paradise unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A “little devil” perched on his shoulder whispers that “It’s better to get them before they get you”; he spends a second imagining forcing Chabashira to resign, then returns to blank thinking.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rates the boys aboard as “beasts—sex-starved carnivores” waiting like predators while the girls chatter — his anthropology of the vacation mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Grades the friendship tiers: at the bottom strata, “low-level friends are only invited ten percent of the time” — and he is the lowly friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Asks after Karuizawa’s recovered underwear and is satisfied with Hirata’s quiet resolution of the fiasco.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Hirata’s invitation as carrying “some kind of ulterior motive” before the ask lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But even if I can bring you both together, things won’t be that easy. Horikita is difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Takes the go-between job while admitting he usually just goes along with whatever Horikita says — “I’ve never really forced my opinion on her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Executes his “Speedy Escape” the moment Karuizawa’s group closes ranks over Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pressed into service as the Horikita bridge over lunch; he takes the ask but not the urgency.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Declines her group, then watches her reclaim Hirata anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.14, 20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The subject of Hirata’s request; he warns she will shut down if she senses manipulation.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"ch 2  the class a leverage  named twice named in ayanokoji s cabin reverie   the leverage that brought him to class a s track","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\">Ch.2: the Class A leverage, named twice<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12, p.34<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie — the leverage that brought him to Class A’s track.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The threat that binds him: she “threatened to expel me from this paradise” unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator contrasts her with Mashima: where she seems “unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative,” he is “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Still holds him with the Class A ultimatum three days after the island test.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0  he pulls ayanokoji to lunch ship cabin  he draws ayanokoji out of his sea gazing and steers him toward lunch  cancelling karuizawa s plan to do it   hmm  you haven t been in the room all this time  have you   you might make more friends if you were a little more proactive  ayanokouji kun  though i suppose it s none of my business   that s not true  though  i mean  you have sudou kun and the guys  and horikita san   i m planning to meet up with karuizawa san and the others at 12 30 to have lunch  do you want to come with  i think it ll be really fun   i can understand that you re feeling hesitant  that s exactly why i want you to rely on me   i can eat with karuizawa san and the others any time  but i haven t really had many opportunities to eat together with you  ayanokouji kun   thank you for helping on the deserted island  i m sorry i didn t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit  ayanokouji kun   even so  i m grateful to you for helping","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13–16<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ship cabin: he draws Ayanokōji out of his sea-gazing and steers him toward lunch, cancelling Karuizawa’s plan to do it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Hmm? You haven’t been in the room all this time, have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “You might make more friends if you were a little more proactive, Ayanokouji-kun. Though I suppose it’s none of my business.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “That’s not true, though. I mean, you have Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m planning to meet up with Karuizawa-san and the others at 12:30 to have lunch. Do you want to come with? I think it’ll be really fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wears “that eternal, optimistic smile” and won’t leave a lone person alone; pushes past the refusals.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can understand that you’re feeling hesitant. That’s exactly why I want you to rely on me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can eat with Karuizawa-san and the others any time, but I haven’t really had many opportunities to eat together with you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Karuizawa to cancel on the spot, despite Ayanokōji’s half-hearted protests.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you for helping on the deserted island. I’m sorry I didn’t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I’m grateful to you for helping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Cancels their lunch without flinching; Ayanokōji expects her to blame him later, and he doesn’t seem to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 0  a passing mention in hirata s inventory named once at the cabin lunch  in hirata s list of the people who treat ayanokoji as a friend","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention in Hirata’s inventory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once at the cabin lunch, in Hirata’s list of the people who treat Ayanokōji as a friend.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata’s line carries him: “you have Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 2  2 0  a passing mention as the culprit named once as the underwear culprit  ayanokoji asks whether karuizawa got hers back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.16<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the underwear culprit; Ayanokōji asks whether Karuizawa got hers back.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata confirms the fallout: naming her resolved things — “When she heard Ibuki-san was the culprit, things went smoothly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0  the ask  be the bridge to horikita top deck restaurant  over lunch he finally names his ask   ayanokoji as the bridge to horikita   honestly  there s something i d like your advice on   i wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach horikita san  after all  class d will have to come together and work hard in the future  and i think horikita san will be indispensable   yes  i do understand  of course  horikita san only opens herself up to you  ayanokouji kun   i should probably reconsider how to do this  horikita san seems very fastidious and hypercritical  how do you manage to get along with her  ayanokouji kun   my plan was really short sighted   when ayanokoji calls the timing too soon   sorry  i invited you out to eat and made it all about me  well  let s eat  shall we","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.17–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Top-deck restaurant: over lunch he finally names his ask — Ayanokōji as the bridge to Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Honestly, there’s something I’d like your advice on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach Horikita-san. After all, Class D will have to come together and work hard in the future, and I think Horikita-san will be indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. I do understand, of course. Horikita-san only opens herself up to you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Wants his own hand hidden — “Then, pretend I never spoke to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> “But I can’t come up with anything else right now. I don’t think I have the confidence to speak with Horikita-san, let alone persuade her. This is my last resort.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should probably reconsider how to do this. Horikita-san seems very fastidious and hypercritical. How do you manage to get along with her, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Has “over forty friends” yet is frustrated at missing a connection with one particular student.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My plan was really short-sighted.” (when Ayanokōji calls the timing too soon)<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I invited you out to eat and made it all about me. Well, let’s eat, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Notices Karuizawa approaching and shoots Ayanokōji a nonplussed look before the girls close ranks.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Wants her friendship first, then a working relationship, and lacks the confidence to ask her directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She arrives with her girls and takes the table back.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 0  a hypothetical at the deck restaurant named once  hypothetically   what he and yamauchi would have done at the deck restaurant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once, hypothetically — what he and Yamauchi would have done at the deck restaurant.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s aside: had they been there, they would have “foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 2  2 0  a hypothetical at the deck restaurant named once  hypothetically   what he and ike would have done at the deck restaurant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once, hypothetically — what he and Ike would have done at the deck restaurant.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s aside: had they been there, they would have “foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 0  she reclaims the table crash of the deck lunch  she arrives with her girls and reclaims hirata from the table ayanokoji just fled   ah  so you re here after all  hirata kun  let s eat lunch together","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crash of the deck lunch: she arrives with her girls and reclaims Hirata from the table Ayanokōji just fled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ah, so you’re here after all, Hirata-kun. Let’s eat lunch together!”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The girls pull chairs from another table, push Ayanokōji away, and circle Hirata — peaceful to noisy in seconds.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Happy and carefree in tone while overriding the cancellation; monopolising him is her default.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes the lunch he cancelled as if it were never made.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Karuizawa Kei’s Soliloquy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 1  the koenji corridor and sakura s call corridor on the third deck  koenji dripping from the pool  the bellhop s fourth warning  and ayanokoji s escape route   do you want something from me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor on the third deck: Kōenji dripping from the pool, the bellhop’s fourth warning, and Ayanokōji’s escape route.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Do you want something from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Throws the bellhop’s warning back at Kōenji — “I passed the ball, if you will” — to engineer his own escape.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the ship’s signboard map and fixes the layout in his head: nine decks plus a roof, guys on the third deck and girls on the fourth, the 24-hour lounge on the first.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes Sakura’s email call rather than kill time alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 1  the wet corridor and the signature corridor by the pool  dripping wet in a bathing suit  a fourth warning from the bellhop  a signature demanded   ha ha ha  it appears you ve found me  eh   i don t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason   do you have a pen and paper on hand   even though it s written on such a cheap notepad  it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future   please don t look so suspicious  i am the man who will carry japan s future on his back   oh ho  why  if it isn t little ayanokouji  hmm  what a coincidence   no  no  i ve no real business with you  i ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates  also  though we are certainly not alike in terms of position  you are my roommate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor by the pool: dripping wet in a bathing suit, a fourth warning from the bellhop, a signature demanded.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Ha ha ha! It appears you’ve found me, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I don’t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Do you have a pen and paper on hand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Signs the bellhop’s notepad “Kouenji Rokusuke” and presents it as a future-valuable gift.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though it’s written on such a cheap notepad, it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t look so suspicious. I am the man who will carry Japan’s future on his back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Repeat offender — this is the fourth hallway stop; believes his autograph outranks the notepad and pen.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator’s standing assessment: “Kouenji was like poison.” Classmates steer clear; even Hirata would be brushed off.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flips his wet hair into Ayanokōji’s face without noticing.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh ho? Why, if it isn’t little Ayanokouji, hmm? What a coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, I’ve no real business with you. I’ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates. Also, though we are certainly not alike in terms of position, you are my roommate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “little Ayanokouji”; confirms the cabin roommate pairing and splashes him mid-sentence.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou shinohara-satsuki ichihashi-ruri maezono ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"ch 2  2 2  the roommate appeal emails ayanokoji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry  flees when kushida appears   wah  a ayanokouji kun   n no  no  i m just kind of strangely nervous is all   ayanokouji kun  you re roommates with hirata kun  kouenji kun  and yukimura kun  right   oh  well  to tell you the truth  i i m a little worried about the people i m sharing a room with   i m not sure  i have mixed feelings  i do want to get along with them  but i also want to be alone  too  i m just hopeless  aren t i   oh  didn t i tell you  shinohara san  ichihashi san  and maezono san   i just thought any advice from you  ayanokouji kun  would be good   i i m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue  you re so busy  ayanokouji kun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.25–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Emails Ayanokōji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry; flees when Kushida appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ichihashi-ruri\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#maezono\">Maezono<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Wah! A-Ayanokouji-kun?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “N-no, no. I’m just kind of strangely nervous is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun, you’re roommates with Hirata-kun, Kouenji-kun, and Yukimura-kun. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Nervous to the point of jolt-like surprise; her normally hunched posture straightens at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Well, to tell you the truth, I…I’m a little worried about the people I’m sharing a room with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not sure. I have mixed feelings. I do want to get along with them, but I also want to be alone, too. I’m just hopeless, aren’t I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Didn’t I tell you? Shinohara-san, Ichihashi-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…just thought any advice from you, Ayanokouji-kun, would be good?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I-I’m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue. You’re so busy, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> “retreated as fast as her legs would carry her” at Kushida’s arrival.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Rejection and flight; Kushida’s brightness lands as threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Names her as roommate one; the narration adds Shinohara won’t go out of her way for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/b> Roommate two — named only; no file yet (first appearance volume).<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Maezono<\/b> Roommate three — named only; no file yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Comes to him because “any advice from you…would be good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 2  sakura s worry  kushida s interrupt  the school message second deck hallway  sakura s roommate appeal  kushida s interruption  the school s test message  and the chat with horikita   you re worried because even though you want to get along with them  you don t think you can   it s no big deal  i don t mind it when you come to me for advice  whether i ll be of much help is another story   i m joking  don t you know by now that i m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff   did you get a message from the school just now   chat line  the corpus prints it bare after  i typed   yeah  i did   untagged chat reply  the thread has only these two   my designated meeting time is 18 00  what about yours   chat   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   untagged chat reply   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   untagged chat reply  the narration marks her replies instant   understood   chat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.26–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck hallway: Sakura’s roommate appeal, Kushida’s interruption, the school’s test message, and the chat with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You’re worried because even though you want to get along with them, you don’t think you can?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s no big deal. I don’t mind it when you come to me for advice. Whether I’ll be of much help is another story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m joking. Don’t you know by now that I’m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Ship cabin roommates: Hirata, Kōenji, and Yukimura — Sakura states it; he doesn’t dispute it.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Compares messages with Kushida: his call is 18:00, hers 20:40, her room two doors down from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you get a message from the school just now?” (chat line; the corpus prints it bare after “I typed.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I did.” (untagged chat reply; the thread has only these two)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My designated meeting time is 18:00. What about yours?” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (untagged chat reply)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (untagged chat reply; the narration marks her replies instant)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Horikita’s instant replies as unusual — she normally waits half a day, sometimes days, to read.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps the Horikita chat to himself when Kushida draws near, deciding to wait and see.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Refuses her Class C outing, lets her see the phone, shares nothing about the chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Receives her roommate appeal; can only offer limited help.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 2  the hallway interrupt and the message compare exits a second deck room into the hallway mid meeting plan  interrupts sakura s appeal  then compares school messages with ayanokoji   huh  ayanokouji kun and sakura san  what are you doing here   ah  did i interrupt  i didn t mean to  i was supposed to meet up with some friends   i ve made plans to go see some girls from class c today  do you want to come  ayanokouji kun   oh jeez  come on  you surprised me a little  ayanokouji kun  you re funny","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.27–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Exits a second-deck room into the hallway mid-meeting-plan; interrupts Sakura’s appeal, then compares school messages with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh? Ayanokouji-kun and Sakura-san? What are you doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Ah, did I interrupt? I didn’t mean to. I was supposed to meet up with some friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’ve made plans to go see some girls from Class C today. Do you want to come, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh jeez, come on. You surprised me a little. Ayanokouji-kun, you’re funny.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her true self “seemed puzzled by my response” when he says yes — the mask slips a little before the smooth recovery.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Without hesitation shows him her message: 20:40, a room two doors from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Draws nearer, curious about his chat with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The bright entrance that sends Sakura fleeing; Kushida apologises to no evident purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Invites, reads his joke, shares her phone, watches his screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 2  2 2  named as sakura s roommate named as sakura s first roommate  with the narration s character sketch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: named as Sakura’s roommate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.27<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as Sakura’s first roommate, with the narration’s character sketch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Roommate; the narration sizes her up — close with Karuizawa, “like her boss, really” — reliable and unafraid of a fight, but relentless against people she doesn’t like, so she “probably wouldn’t go out of her way to befriend her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 2  the message chat chat only  ayanokoji messages her about the school s test notice  she replies instantly   yeah  i did   chat reply  the translation leaves the thread s lines untagged   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   chat   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   chat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.30–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chat only: Ayanokōji messages her about the school’s test notice; she replies instantly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yeah. I did.” (chat reply; the translation leaves the thread’s lines untagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Replies instantly — against her usual half-day, sometimes days, reading lag.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two further chat lines sit unassigned in the translation: “I’m curious about the difference in start times…” and “We can’t know anything for sure at this point.” The volume attribution list keeps them.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Off-page: Hirata’s whole lunch ask is about winning her over, routed through Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chat partner with the earlier slot; she defers his report.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action","w":"sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the zodiac briefing opens room 204 on the second deck  mashima s briefing table  sotomura and yukimura already seated  karuizawa as the late fourth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Room 204 on the second deck: Mashima’s briefing table, Sotomura and Yukimura already seated, Karuizawa as the late fourth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sotomura-hideo\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Takes the vacant seat beside Yukimura and waits out the unseen fourth member.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the setup as ominous — small groups, private rooms, a teacher who won’t take questions: “There was a storm coming, the curtain rising on a new test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Classmate at the table; the Professor greets him with “Ayanokouji-dono.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The roommate beside him; he stays quiet while Yukimura and Karuizawa trade blows.<span class=\"pg\">p.32, 36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer: cold, unanswerable, “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The fourth member; she moves her chair away from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 3  the zodiac briefing briefs the four class d students in room 204  zodiac groups  thinking tested four ways   what are you doing  hurry and take a seat   we are still waiting on one more  please sit quietly   i believe you were told punctuality was key  and yet you re late  hurry and take your seat   sotomura  yukimura  ayanokouji  and karuizawa  from class d  without further ado  i will now explain the special test   i will not answer any questions at this time  be quiet and listen   in this special test  all the first year students will be divided into twelve groups based on the signs of the zodiac   society needs three fundamental qualities in order to progress  action  thinking  and teamwork  those with the necessary qualities will become wonderful adults   i ve already told you  i will not be answering any questions   you four gathered here will be in the same group  at this very moment  students in other rooms are receiving the same explanation you are   calm down  you two  yukimura  your concerns are groundless  the test hasn t yet begun  so you won t be affected  besides  your attitude has no bearing on this test","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Briefs the four Class D students in Room 204: zodiac groups, thinking tested four ways.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “What are you doing? Hurry and take a seat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “We are still waiting on one more. Please sit quietly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “I believe you were told punctuality was key, and yet you’re late. Hurry and take your seat”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sotomura, Yukimura, Ayanokouji, and Karuizawa, from Class D. Without further ado, I will now explain the special test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will not answer any questions at this time. Be quiet and listen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this special test, all the first-year students will be divided into twelve groups based on the signs of the Zodiac.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Names the four tested abilities: processing information, analyzing the situation, solving after clarifying, and creating new values through imagination.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Society needs three fundamental qualities in order to progress: action, thinking, and teamwork. Those with the necessary qualities will become wonderful adults.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already told you. I will not be answering any questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You four gathered here will be in the same group. At this very moment, students in other rooms are receiving the same explanation you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, you two. Yukimura, your concerns are groundless. The test hasn’t yet begun, so you won’t be affected. Besides, your attitude has no bearing on this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold and unanswerable; the narrator pits him against Chabashira — she “unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative,” he “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The comparison the narrator draws between the two homeroom instructors.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns her twice before shutting her questions down.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 2  2 3  the professor at the briefing table already seated in room 204 beside yukimura when ayanokoji arrives for the zodiac briefing   so  one of the remaining two spots belongs to ayanokouji dono  i see  most agreeable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor at the briefing table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sotomura-hideo\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Already seated in Room 204 beside Yukimura when Ayanokōji arrives for the zodiac briefing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “So, one of the remaining two spots belongs to Ayanokouji-dono, I see! Most agreeable!”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Introduced as “The Professor”: overweight first-year in glasses, the male-otaku stereotype, deep in history and machinery — though his speech and inflection come off unintelligible, he somehow communicates.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Silent through the whole briefing and the Karuizawa–Yukimura quarrel; “The Professor and I stayed quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Greets him with the nerdy “Ayanokouji-dono.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The unexpected pairing — the narrator notes the Professor and Yukimura don’t normally sit together.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  odd company  first quarrel seated at mashima s table with the professor  first to spot that the gathering is odd   this is rather odd  isn t it  ayanokouji   how about you shut up and try listening  the test is probably going to start soon  if they dock our points because you keep blabbing  are you gonna take responsibility   even back on the deserted island  you dragged us all down  can you try not to cause any more problems","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32, p.36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Seated at Mashima’s table with the Professor; first to spot that the gathering is odd.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sotomura-hideo\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “This is rather odd, isn’t it? Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “How about you shut up and try listening? The test is probably going to start soon. If they dock our points because you keep blabbing, are you gonna take responsibility?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Even back on the deserted island, you dragged us all down. Can you try not to cause any more problems?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> First to lose patience with Karuizawa; point-anxious and practical.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Trades insults with her under the teacher’s eye.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Paired oddly at the table, by the narrator’s note.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the fourth seat of the zodiac group fourth seat of the class d zodiac group  arrives to find three boys and a teacher  and questions it immediately   huh  what s going on  why are yukimura kun and these other guys here   w wait a minute  i don t understand  what do you mean  explain a test  the test was already over  right  also  what s the deal with these guys  this is really weird   jeez  all right  fine  i ll shut up   what do you mean by  test our thinking   i don t get what any of this means  can you explain it in a way that s easier to understand   these guys gross me out  why am i on a team together with boys  honestly  i hate it though being with hirata kun would be fine   huh  when and how exactly did i cause problems  you re pissing me off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.33–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fourth seat of the Class D zodiac group; arrives to find three boys and a teacher, and questions it immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Huh? What’s going on? Why are Yukimura-kun and these other guys here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “W-wait a minute. I don’t understand. What do you mean, explain a test? The test was already over, right? Also, what’s the deal with these guys? This is really weird.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Jeez, all right. Fine, I’ll shut up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Studies the three boys, then lifts her chair and moves it away from Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean by ‘test our thinking’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t get what any of this means. Can you explain it in a way that’s easier to understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “These guys gross me out. Why am I on a team together with boys? Honestly, I hate it…though being with Hirata-kun would be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? When and how exactly did I cause problems? You’re pissing me off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Barrages the teacher until told to be quiet twice; complies unhappily; blunt about the boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> His “you dragged us all down” lands; she fires back that he’s pissing her off.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Defies the cold briefer, then submits.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The only boy on the team she’ll tolerate.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the four outcomes and the traitor rules still at mashima s table  the group roster  the handout of four outcomes  and the werewolf detour  all read through ayanokoji s eyes   karuizawa  if you don t change your attitude toward the teachers  it might leave a mark on your permanent record  that wouldn t be good  right  reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head  with answers accepted any time  no one would seriously aim for outcome  1  reduces the exam to four possibilities   the honest outcome  1  a wrong guess at the end  the traitor finding the vip  and the traitor misled   and wants to avoid the last one most of all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still at Mashima’s table: the group roster, the handout of four outcomes, and the Werewolf detour, all read through Ayanokōji’s eyes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Karuizawa, if you don’t change your attitude toward the teachers, it might leave a mark on your permanent record. That wouldn’t be good, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head: with answers accepted any time, no one would seriously aim for Outcome #1.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reduces the exam to four possibilities — the honest Outcome #1, a wrong guess at the end, the traitor finding the VIP, and the traitor misled — and wants to avoid the last one most of all.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Depressed hearing Karuizawa rank the three of them below Hirata, though he tries not to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Knows Ichinose from Class B and Ibuki from Class C off the printed roster; of Ibuki he thinks being in the same group “was a perverse kind of fate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has never heard of the party game Werewolf — Karuizawa’s amazement lands on genuine ignorance.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Easily memorizes the prohibited-actions list: phone theft, threats for VIP information, impersonation by borrowed phone, and cross-class discussion until the exam ends — each punishable up to expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the school’s anonymity design means any school-sent message is “100% the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns her about her permanent record; she brushes it off.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer he watches absorb Karuizawa’s interruptions without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari sotomura-hideo hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the interrupter  the werewolf  the phone call through the briefing she trades smirks with yukimura  interrupts mashima repeatedly  learns the four outcomes  and finally phones hirata   hmph   after ayanokoji s warning about her permanent record   ugh  jeez  this sucks  i can t deal with these three  hirata kun would have been so much better   gross  even if there were a hundred or two hundred of you  you still wouldn t be worth a single hair on hirata kun s head   to the professor   ugh  well  at any rate  i ll just report it to hirata kun later   okay  okay  i understand that we re being divided into these groups  but why is it only the four of us getting this explanation  i thought you d explain things after our entire group was gathered together   w wait a minute  what do you mean  i still don t get it at all  we re going to be grouped with students from other classes  isn t that crazy  though  aren t the other classes supposed to be the enemy   jeez  everyone s gonna be jealous of the vip  not being picked for it would be unfair  no matter what happens  that person still gets points  and if we get outcome  1  it s a million points   wait a second  ayanokouji kun  don t tell me you don t know about werewolf  whoa  i can t believe it   i m sorry  it s just  like  not having friends must be so sad   when his ignorance shows   well  you get together with your friends  and then you divide people up as either villagers or wolves  the one who survives at the end is th","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–50<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Through the briefing she trades smirks with Yukimura, interrupts Mashima repeatedly, learns the four outcomes, and finally phones Hirata.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sotomura-hideo\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hmph.” (after Ayanokōji’s warning about her permanent record)<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ugh, jeez! This sucks! I can’t deal with these three! Hirata-kun would have been so much better!”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Gross. Even if there were a hundred or two hundred of you, you still wouldn’t be worth a single hair on Hirata-kun’s head.” (to the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ugh. Well, at any rate, I’ll just report it to Hirata-kun later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, okay. I understand that we’re being divided into these groups, but why is it only the four of us getting this explanation? I thought you’d explain things after our entire group was gathered together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait a minute. What do you mean? I still don’t get it at all. We’re going to be grouped with students from other classes? Isn’t that crazy, though? Aren’t the other classes supposed to be the enemy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jeez, everyone’s gonna be jealous of the VIP! Not being picked for it would be unfair! No matter what happens, that person still gets points! And if we get Outcome #1, it’s a million points!”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Half-listens so hard her comprehension goes “abnormally bad” — the narration contrasts her with Sudō and Ike, who score poorly, versus her refusal to listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a second. Ayanokouji-kun, don’t tell me you don’t know about Werewolf? Whoa, I can’t believe it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. It’s just, like, not having friends must be so sad.” (when his ignorance shows)<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you get together with your friends, and then you divide people up as either villagers or wolves. The one who survives at the end is the winner. Get it?” (explaining Werewolf)<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And that’s…on the other side of the handout, right? Is it okay if we turn it over?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm, umm. I kind of get it, but I kind of don’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, we can’t leave the room? How long do we need to stay in there?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agh. Well, this sounds kinda annoying, but I guess I do understand somewhat. Ugh. I just wish we had a test that was more fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ignores Yukimura’s huddle pitch, takes out her phone mid-hallway, and calls Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, hi, Hirata-kun? There was something I wanted to talk to you about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Trades barbs with him from the first smirks to the hallway dismissal.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Interrupts him four times; he answers without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The “hundred or two hundred of you” line lands on the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The call she makes the moment the briefing ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 3  the handout and the four outcomes carries the briefing to its end  cross class groups  the printed roster  the vip handout  werewolf  and the meeting logistics   listen  your group assignments are a done deal  you cannot change them  to gain a good result on the test  you must get along   finished  please let me continue my explanation   it would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering  therefore  i will try to provide an answer  this is neither a conspiracy against the students  nor is it harassment  it s rather simple  the groups don t consist of members from just one class  they are made up of about three to five individuals collected from each class  if we didn t explain things in advance  we would run the risk of confusion   you ve been competing until now  your school lives have only just begun  you shouldn t run around like a chicken with its head cut off this early  yukimura   right now  you shouldn t spend your energy on trying to understand this test  rather  focus on how to think  your group assignment is  rabbit  here is a list of the members  you will be required to return this list when you leave the room  if you feel it s necessary  i would recommend trying to memorize it now   don t worry  i will answer any questions you have  i believe you will be able to understand everything afterward  probably   the point of this test is to ignore the prior fraught relationships between classes a through d  if you do  you ll have a s","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Carries the briefing to its end: cross-class groups, the printed roster, the VIP handout, Werewolf, and the meeting logistics.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Listen. Your group assignments are a done deal. You cannot change them. To gain a good result on the test, you must get along.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Finished? Please let me continue my explanation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “It would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering. Therefore, I will try to provide an answer. This is neither a conspiracy against the students, nor is it harassment. It’s rather simple. The groups…”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering. Therefore, I will try to provide an answer. This is neither a conspiracy against the students, nor is it harassment. It’s rather simple. The groups don’t consist of members from just one class; they are made up of about three to five individuals collected from each class. If we didn’t explain things in advance, we would run the risk of confusion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been competing until now? Your school lives have only just begun. You shouldn’t run around like a chicken with its head cut off this early, Yukimura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right now, you shouldn’t spend your energy on trying to understand this test. Rather, focus on how to think. Your group assignment is ‘Rabbit’. Here is a list of the members. You will be required to return this list when you leave the room. If you feel it’s necessary, I would recommend trying to memorize it now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I will answer any questions you have. I believe you will be able to understand everything afterward. Probably.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The point of this test is to ignore the prior fraught relationships between Classes A through D. If you do, you’ll have a shortcut.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From this point on, you are no longer acting as members of Class D, but rather as members of the Rabbit group. Whether you pass or fail this test depends on each group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Four outcomes only; handouts of the grade items may be verified on the spot but not taken, photographed, or copied.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The test runs from 8:00 a.m. day one’s message to 9:00 p.m. day four; two one-hour group meetings daily at set times and rooms; answers accepted only 9:30–10:00 p.m. the final night, by email, first submission per group counts, one answer per student, VIPs may not submit, results emailed 11:00 p.m.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outcome #1: a correct final answer pays every group member 500,000 private points. Outcome #2: no or wrong final submission pays only the VIP 500,000.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This exam has one critical element. Understand it, and this test will not pose a problem. The key element is the existence of the VIP. There is only one VIP in the group. In this test, you’re after the name of the VIP. It’s that simple. For example, Yukimura, let’s say that you were chosen as VIP. The correct answer for the Rabbit group would be ‘Yukimura.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now then, as for Outcome #2… In the event that the VIP’s identity is not discovered before the end of the examination, and no one in your group found out the identity of the VIP or some even attempted to lie about the identity, then only the VIP will be awarded points, just as it says. He or she will receive 500,000 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you understand the explanation for the first two? If you do not, then we cannot continue.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Regarding the remaining outcomes, they are written on the reverse side of the handout. However, please wait a bit before turning the paper over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Very well, I will explain in simpler terms. Have you played the game Werewolf?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I said that there is only one VIP in the group, if the VIP is exposed right away, then Outcomes #3 and #4 will appear.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outcome #3: an early correct answer by a non-VIP pays that student 500,000 private points and their class 50 class points, costs the VIP’s class 50, and ends the group’s test — a VIP-classmate’s early correct answer doesn’t count. Outcome #4: an early wrong answer by a non-VIP costs their class 50 class points and pays the VIP 500,000 plus 50 to the VIP’s class — a VIP-classmate’s early wrong answer doesn’t count.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school will take anonymity into account during this test. At the end, only the outcomes for each group and the increase or decrease in points for each class will be announced. In other words, we will not announce the names of the VIPs or those who submitted answers. Also, if you wish, you may have a temporary ID assigned to you, to which you can transfer points. It is also possible to divide points up and receive them that way. If you yourself remain quiet, there should be no fear of discovery after the test. Of course, if it’s not necessary for you to hide your identity, you may receive your points openly. That is perfectly fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Outcomes #3 and #4 are very different from the first two. That’s why they are listed on the reverse side of the sheet. With that, the explanation is complete.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There should also be a list of prohibited actions on the sheet. Make sure to examine it thoroughly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Prohibited: stealing phones, threats to confirm VIP information, using another’s phone to submit — up to expulsion; cross-class discussion until the exam ends — expulsion; school messages may not be copied, deleted, transferred, or modified.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tomorrow, you will go to your designated room at 1:00 p.m. and again at 8:00 p.m. Your group’s name will be displayed on a nameplate… Be sure to introduce yourselves when you meet the other members for the first time. After you’ve entered, leaving the room during the examination is not permitted. Please use the restroom ahead of time. In the event that you feel ill or can’t endure it any longer, please contact your homeroom teacher immediately and make a request.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49-50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The explanation is written on the sheet. The discussion period is for one hour. Aside from self-introduction upon your initial meeting, you are free to use that time however you like. Once the hour has passed, you are free to remain in the room or to leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school is committed to fairness, so we will be strict and impartial. After the VIP has been selected, we will not accept any changes, not even if the VIP wants to be changed. In addition, copying, deleting, transferring, or modifying emails sent from the school is prohibited. Understand these points clearly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Flat, unchanging tone throughout; sharp-eyed when they reach for the paper — “It seemed like the exam had already begun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Absorbs her four interruptions without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cuts his chicken-with-its-head-short speech down.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 2  2 3  the professor s interjections three appearances inside the briefing day  the three heads quip  the confused handout  and the anime powered exit   heh  but you know  three heads are better than one  thus  if the three of us join together  we might be able to surpass the good hirata dono  my dear lady   this has turned into quite a bothersome ordeal  being partnered with a bitch like that  i mean   after karuizawa s call   that is certainly true  hmm  she s an unforgivable bitch  she s a bitch among bitches  wouldn t you say   agreeing with yukimura   i am terribly sorry  but i must decline your invitation  for you see  the love love alive anime calls  and i cannot afford to miss its siren song  i bid you farewell  hi ya","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37, p.41, p.51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sotomura-hideo\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three appearances inside the briefing day: the three-heads quip, the confused handout, and the anime-powered exit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Heh. But you know, three heads are better than one. Thus, if the three of us join together, we might be able to surpass the good Hirata-dono, my dear lady,”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “This has turned into quite a bothersome ordeal. Being partnered with a bitch like that, I mean,” (after Karuizawa’s call)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “That is certainly true, hmm? She’s an unforgivable bitch. She’s a bitch among bitches, wouldn’t you say?” (agreeing with Yukimura)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Cocked his head over the handout alongside Karuizawa, “as if wracking their brains.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am terribly sorry, but I must decline your invitation. For you see, the Love Love Alive anime calls, and I cannot afford to miss its siren song. I bid you farewell. Hi-ya!”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration notes he often claims he wants the 2D world and that 2D women are perfect — which is why real girls like Karuizawa are rejected outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Echoes his exact “space cadets” line from minutes earlier, then turns down his huddle for anime.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Mocks her with the three-heads line, then insults her out of earshot.<span class=\"pg\">p.37, 51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor at the briefing table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the quarrel at the table spends the briefing trading barbs with karuizawa and absorbing mashima s rebuke   i  p pardon me   after mashima cuts him off   karuizawa  please  i m begging you  shut up and listen  i can t concentrate when you prattle on   you two are idiots  i ll explain it later  so don t keep bothering mashima sensei   shooting down karuizawa and the professor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–46<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spends the briefing trading barbs with Karuizawa and absorbing Mashima’s rebuke.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I… P-pardon me.” (after Mashima cuts him off)<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Karuizawa, please. I’m begging you, shut up and listen. I can’t concentrate when you prattle on”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You two are idiots. I’ll explain it later, so don’t keep bothering Mashima-sensei.” (shooting down Karuizawa and the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snorted derisively at Karuizawa without saying a word.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “seemed like he wanted to cozy up to school officials” — the narration’s read on why he polices the others’ questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The main target of his exasperation.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The teacher he stammers an apology to.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami","q":"ch 2  named on the rabbit roster twice named without a scene  on the printed rabbit group roster  and in kanzaki s portrait of a trusted class b boy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\">Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.39, p.56<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Twice named without a scene: on the printed Rabbit group roster, and in Kanzaki’s portrait of a trusted Class B boy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed among the three Class B members of the Rabbit group — Ayanokōji knows her by name off the sheet.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kanzaki is described as the Class B student whom “Ichinose—Class B’s leader—seemed to trust.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Her trust is the credential the narration gives him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 3  a passing mention in the comprehension sketch named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up karuizawa s refusal to listen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up Karuizawa’s refusal to listen.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The comparison: her problem “wasn’t that she scored poorly on tests like Sudou or Ike” — unlike them, she simply won’t listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 3  a passing mention in the comprehension sketch named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up karuizawa s refusal to listen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up Karuizawa’s refusal to listen.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The comparison: her problem “wasn’t that she scored poorly on tests like Sudou or Ike” — unlike them, she simply won’t listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention in Hirata’s inventory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the failed huddle in the room and then the hallway  he probes ayanokoji  pitches a three man plan  and watches it dissolve   hey  ayanokouji  you ve been quiet  do you actually understand everything   for crying out loud  why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   said once in the room   why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   repeated in the hallway  word for word   i hate to say this  but if we have to be in the same group  we need to put up a unified front  a lot of things will depend on who the vip is  but for now  the four of us should discuss things   h hey  karuizawa  are you listening   maybe in the morning there ll be a notification that one of us was chosen as the vip  if one of us is chosen  it d be smart not to spread it around carelessly  we don t know who might be listening  let s get to a secure location before sharing info   to be honest  i really hate it  no matter what i do  she ll only drag us down   on karuizawa   karuizawa may be gone  but i want to talk about tomorrow  it makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us  let s go","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.49–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the room and then the hallway: he probes Ayanokōji, pitches a three-man plan, and watches it dissolve.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sotomura-hideo\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Hey, Ayanokouji. You’ve been quiet. Do you actually understand everything?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “For crying out loud, why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (said once in the room)<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (repeated in the hallway, word for word)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hate to say this, but if we have to be in the same group, we need to put up a unified front. A lot of things will depend on who the VIP is, but for now, the four of us should discuss things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-hey, Karuizawa. Are you listening?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe in the morning there’ll be a notification that one of us was…chosen as the VIP. If one of us is chosen, it’d be smart not to spread it around carelessly. We don’t know who might be listening. Let’s get to a secure location before sharing info.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50-51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I really hate it. No matter what I do, she’ll only drag us down.” (on Karuizawa)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa may be gone, but I want to talk about tomorrow. It makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us. Let’s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sighs and shakes it off when the Professor declines and Ayanokōji doesn’t engage — “He didn’t seem to want to work with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her phone call kills the huddle; he vents about her afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The invitee who bows out for Love Love Alive.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Probes whether he understood the briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the hallway split leaving mashima s room  yukimura s huddle plan collapses when karuizawa calls hirata and the professor declines   for the most part  i guess  i d like you to explain the things i don t fully understand later  though   to yukimura  who asked whether he understood","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.50–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaving Mashima’s room: Yukimura’s huddle plan collapses when Karuizawa calls Hirata and the Professor declines.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “For the most part, I guess. I’d like you to explain the things I don’t fully understand later, though.” (to Yukimura, who asked whether he understood)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Feigns incompleteness on purpose — “I wasn’t going to tell Hirata anything more” in the later hallway talk — and lets Yukimura’s discontent pass unnoticed.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Agrees the ship may be bugged, accepts Yukimura’s secure-location plan in principle, then reports the Rabbit rules to Horikita by chat and starts shaping a strategy alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The one classmate who tries to build a three-man huddle with him; Yukimura sighs and drops it.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 5  the katsuragi warning and the cold exit off screen first   ayanokoji reports the rabbit rules to her by chat   then on the second deck she faces katsuragi  holds against kanzaki s interlude  and turns her back on ryuen   yes  i am  and what exactly does that have to do with you   to katsuragi   you wanted to speak with me  funny  didn t you completely ignore me the other day   that s rather petty  from class a s perspective  are we such a big deal  i mean  there s a significant gap in points between us   you needn t concern yourself  class d has always been regarded as inferior  i d welcome any change in our reputation   what do you mean   when katsuragi calls the island win luck   we haven t gotten into college yet  i don t think you and i are so different  the school arbitrarily divided us into different classes  don t forget that   if we re going to continue this pointless conversation  i d prefer to just go inside  besides  it s about time   flipping her hair away from ryuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.51, p.55–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Off-screen first — Ayanokōji reports the Rabbit rules to her by chat — then on the second deck she faces Katsuragi, holds against Kanzaki’s interlude, and turns her back on Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yes, I am. And what exactly does that have to do with you?” (to Katsuragi)<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You wanted to speak with me? Funny. Didn’t you completely ignore me the other day?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s rather petty. From Class A’s perspective, are we such a big deal? I mean, there’s a significant gap in points between us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Receives his chat report on the Rabbit group’s rules; her reply is not printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You needn’t concern yourself. Class D has always been regarded as inferior. I’d welcome any change in our reputation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?” (when Katsuragi calls the island win luck)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We haven’t gotten into college yet. I don’t think you and I are so different. The school arbitrarily divided us into different classes. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we’re going to continue this pointless conversation, I’d prefer to just go inside. Besides, it’s about time.” (flipping her hair away from Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t back down before the Class A entourage; the narration credits her — weak-willed students would ingratiate themselves, she acts as she always does.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads her own new reputation: other classes now treat her selfishness as class concern and fear her as a hidden mastermind.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The pivot from his island-test indifference to a Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Declines his rescue — “You needn’t concern yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Exits on him mid-provocation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Both summoned to the 20:40 meeting (see Hirata’s row).<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations just before 20 30 he wakes in the third deck cabin to hirata s apology  and they step out together toward the evening s meetings   can t really say  i haven t been thinking about the exam like you  horikita  and yukimura have  i m not smart  either  so i haven t really noticed much   deflecting hirata s request for observations   yeah  i think you re right  hirata  it would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time  rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages  suspects the school s deliberately scattered briefings mean their  thinking  is already being tested","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Just before 20:30 he wakes in the third-deck cabin to Hirata’s apology, and they step out together toward the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Can’t really say. I haven’t been thinking about the exam like you, Horikita, and Yukimura have. I’m not smart, either, so I haven’t really noticed much.” (deflecting Hirata’s request for observations)<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah, I think you’re right, Hirata. It would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time, rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Suspects the school’s deliberately scattered briefings mean their “thinking” is already being tested.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Walks him to the second deck while sharing nothing of substance.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations in the third deck cabin he straightens his luggage  puts on his uniform  and wakes ayanokoji for the evening s meetings   i m sorry  did i wake you   would you like to come with me  i was thinking the school s message should be coming pretty soon   did you notice anything  ayanokouji kun  if it s okay  i d like you to share it with me   well  i was wondering why the explanations are so scattered  i thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group  but after thinking about it  i don t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the third-deck cabin he straightens his luggage, puts on his uniform, and wakes Ayanokōji for the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’m sorry. Did I wake you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Would you like to come with me? I was thinking the school’s message should be coming pretty soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Did you notice anything, Ayanokouji-kun? If it’s okay, I’d like you to share it with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Already knows the test’s specifics — Yukimura told him over their meal — and several students have come to talk it through with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I was wondering why the explanations are so…scattered. I thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group, but after thinking about it, I don’t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Plans to ask a teacher directly about the staged briefings.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Wakes him, walks him down, gets only a deflection for his troubles.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> His inside source on the Rabbit rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin at 20 30  the narration notes the room s other occupants are gone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin at 20:30, the narration notes the room’s other occupants are gone.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Neither Yukimura nor Kouenji were in the room.” — absent from the third-deck cabin while Hirata straightens his luggage.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin  neither he nor koenji is there","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin, neither he nor Kōenji is there.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Absent from the third-deck cabin at 20:30 — Ayanokōji notes the room holds only himself and Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 5  the 20 40 gathering at the second deck meeting place he watches katsuragi confront horikita  kanzaki intercede  ryuen prowl  and kushida arrive puzzled   who are those people   asking hirata to name the waiting students  notes katsuragi s entourage and horikita s changed standing  other classes now see her as  a puppet master  a mastermind who worked behind the scenes  credits horikita s cold shoulder resilience   the island win is his  but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden  expects a huge showdown between katsuragi and ryuen before the test begins  it doesn t come   well then  good luck   leaving hirata at the gathering","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the second-deck meeting place he watches Katsuragi confront Horikita, Kanzaki intercede, Ryūen prowl, and Kushida arrive puzzled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Who are those people?” (asking Hirata to name the waiting students)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes Katsuragi’s entourage and Horikita’s changed standing: other classes now see her as “a puppet master, a mastermind who worked behind the scenes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well then, good luck.” (leaving Hirata at the gathering)<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Burns Morimiya and Tokitō’s names and faces into memory on Hirata’s tip, then keeps to the line without making a fuss.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Credits Horikita’s cold-shoulder resilience — the island win is his, but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Expects a huge showdown between Katsuragi and Ryūen before the test begins; it doesn’t come.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Stands by as Katsuragi threatens her class and Kanzaki pulls him off; impressed she won’t be shaken.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Watches the Class A leader pivot from ignoring Horikita to warning her.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Notes the demented chuckle and the docile lackeys trailing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Present when she wanders into the gathering, puzzled.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 5  the 20 40 gathering second deck meeting place  he names the waiting students for ayanokoji  then stands inside the katsuragi horikita ryuen current   it doesn t seem like all of these people are in my group   that s morimiya kun  from class a  and that one near the elevator is tokitou kun  from class c   the well connected answer   yes  though if i m with you  kanzaki kun  and katsuragi kun  struggle has to be inevitable   answering kanzaki s sympathy   don t worry  no matter who is in my group  i ll do my best   to katsuragi  positive as always","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck meeting place: he names the waiting students for Ayanokōji, then stands inside the Katsuragi–Horikita–Ryūen current.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It doesn’t seem like all of these people are in my group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “That’s Morimiya-kun, from Class A. And that one near the elevator is Tokitou-kun, from Class C.” (the well-connected answer)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. Though if I’m with you, Kanzaki-kun, and Katsuragi-kun, struggle has to be inevitable.” (answering Kanzaki’s sympathy)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. No matter who is in my group, I’ll do my best.” (to Katsuragi, positive as always)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Positive through the threat display; Kushida reads his steadiness as the sign that the battle will be grueling.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Addressed as the group’s Class A anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The Class B boy who spots him landed in trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She finds him amid the gathering and takes his composure for reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Both summoned to the same 20:40 meeting — the team Katsuragi named.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 2  2 5  the class a pivot on horikita at the 20 40 gathering he singles horikita out of the line  then holds court against her  kanzaki  and ryuen   unless i m mistaken  you re also in the group meeting at 20 40  yes   that s good news  i wanted to speak with you again  i m also in the 20 40 group  starting tomorrow  we will be working together   you re correct  i certainly haven t acknowledged anyone in class d until now  however  considering the incredible results from the last test  it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you  wouldn t you agree  you laid the groundwork to win  and succeeded handsomely   i don t know what the future might hold  but should class d overtake class c  know that class a would attack you without mercy   that s certainly true  however  we must be cautious  it s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up  if one class manages to change its station  we must be vigilant  i would give the same warning to both classes b and c   however  just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn t make us equals   anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck  it s better that you don t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance  remember that the difference in our class points is still massive   that s a rather deplorable thing to say  especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures  you realize that ja","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Class A pivot on Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the 20:40 gathering he singles Horikita out of the line, then holds court against her, Kanzaki, and Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Unless I’m mistaken, you’re also in the group meeting at 20:40, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “That’s good news. I wanted to speak with you again. I’m also in the 20:40 group. Starting tomorrow, we will be working together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You…”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You laid the groundwork to win, and succeeded handsomely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what the future might hold, but…should Class D overtake Class C, know that Class A would attack you without mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s certainly true. However, we must be cautious. It’s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up. If one class manages to change its station, we must be vigilant. I would give the same warning to both Classes B and C.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn’t make us equals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck. It’s better that you don’t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance. Remember that the difference in our class points is still massive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a rather deplorable thing to say. Especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures. You realize that Japan is often referred to as an academic society?” (to Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t let you bring your awful attitude to this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it doesn’t matter. Since we’re in the same group now, we’ll be able to talk at length.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay, Hirata? I think this is going to be an especially grueling battle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and collected to a degree that reads as college-age; “most had already acknowledged him as their leader” — the Class A entourage glares on cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Dismissive gesture “like he was brushing dirt off his clothes” while calling the island win luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The pivot from island-test indifference to a formal Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Brushed off by him, then trading academic-ability arguments with Ryūen in front of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The “Beauty and the Beast” provocation and the awful-attitude standoff.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him the group’s grinding battle ahead.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 2  2 5  the class b interlude walks quietly past katsuragi s entourage to pull the heat off horikita  then greets hirata s arrival   i don t much like ganging up on people  or threatening other classes   you don t need to waste time on katsuragi  he s just trying to get to you   to horikita  gentlemanly despite not being on good terms with her   hirata  looks like you landed in a troublesome group   oh  i don t think so   when hirata says struggle with him  kanzaki  and katsuragi is inevitable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Class B interlude<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.56–57<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks quietly past Katsuragi’s entourage to pull the heat off Horikita, then greets Hirata’s arrival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “I don’t much like ganging up on people, or threatening other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “You don’t need to waste time on Katsuragi. He’s just trying to get to you.” (to Horikita, gentlemanly despite not being on good terms with her)<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Hirata, looks like you landed in a troublesome group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I don’t think so.” (when Hirata says struggle with him, Kanzaki, and Katsuragi is inevitable)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Honest type — long hair without slacker energy; the narration notes Ichinose, Class B’s leader, seems to trust him, and that he faced Horikita once during the summer vacation and knows her intellect.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Rescues her from the gang-up, declined without heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Interrupts his threat display; later stands by through the Ryūen exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Reads his group as trouble at a glance.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as the Class B leader who trusts him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 2  2 5  the walk through provocation arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys  sizes up the pond  and picks a fight with katsuragi   well  well  so many fish in this pond  i ve come to take a look for myself   unfortunately  it looks like i m with you   to katsuragi s question whether he belongs to the meeting   how about you put on a little show for me  what do you think of beauty and the beast   looking at both horikita and katsuragi  then letting out a demented little chuckle   academic ability  how droll  that kind of thing is meaningless   hmm  awful attitude  what in the world are you talking about  i can t possibly imagine  can you perhaps tell me how i am  in fact  awful","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.57–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys, sizes up the pond, and picks a fight with Katsuragi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Well, well. So many fish in this pond. I’ve come to take a look for myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Unfortunately, it looks like I’m with you.” (to Katsuragi’s question whether he belongs to the meeting)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “How about you put on a little show for me? What do you think of Beauty and the Beast?” (looking at both Horikita and Katsuragi, then letting out a demented little chuckle)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Academic ability? How droll. That kind of thing is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm? Awful attitude? What in the world are you talking about? I can’t possibly imagine. Can you perhaps tell me how I am, in fact, awful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gestured to his crew as if to ask whether Katsuragi’s argument was believable; “their response mechanical.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His three followers wear terrified looks and move docile — “more like a king and his servants.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The academic-society argument ends in a cold stalemate.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She flips her hair and turns her back on him to go inside.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 5  the puzzled arrival wanders into the 20 40 gathering without understanding the group structure  then reads the room fast enough to keep up   huh  hirata kun  oh  ayanokouji kun  too  what are you all doing here   hmm  group  i don t understand  i did get an email telling me to come here at this time  wow  there really are some amazing people here  huh   um  well  so  it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way   ah ha  don t worry  it s okay  like hirata kun said  all i can do is my best  oh  i haven t really had many chances to talk with katsuragi kun and ryuuen kun yet  i d like to get along with you all  too   speaking to everyone present","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.60–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wanders into the 20:40 gathering without understanding the group structure, then reads the room fast enough to keep up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh, Hirata-kun? Oh, Ayanokouji-kun, too? What are you all doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Hmm? Group? I don’t understand. I did get an email telling me to come here at this time… Wow, there really are some amazing people here, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Um, well. So, it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Somewhat taken back yet respectful of everyone gathered; by fragments of conversation she begins to grasp the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah ha! Don’t worry, it’s okay! Like Hirata-kun said, all I can do is my best. Oh, I haven’t really had many chances to talk with Katsuragi-kun and Ryuuen-kun yet. I’d like to get along with you all, too.” (speaking to everyone present)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Delivers the last line without anxiety, disgust, displeasure, or joy in her voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes his composure as her anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names him as someone she hasn’t talked to yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Names him the same way, in the same breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present for her cold exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
